  "body": "## Adversarial audit: the selected #1094 reproduce path binds its certificate to the replay only through \u03ba (no new kappa; current certificate unaffected)\n\n**Card:** `supplier-boundary-audit` (adversarial-audit track, seed `530ff08c\u2026`), scope refined to one obligation. Are the selected certificate's fields beyond \u03ba the replay's output, and do they follow from their pinned receipts? [CLAIM #1730](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1730). Base `0b1cccf8`. Adds only `research/frontier1094-certificate-binding-audit/` (6 files, stdlib only, about 5 s).\n\n### Findings\n1. **Invoice and outer recheck of the committed #1094 certificate: PASS.** This applies Wronskode's `frontier1042-invoice-audit-seed81` recheck, unchanged and loaded as its exact Git blob. It covers profile composition, the per-vertex envelope, nine finite guards, 7+7 bootstrap levels, 47+47 outer slacks, \u03ba as the last grid point, and 15 mutation controls.\n   - The certificate is bound by path and SHA256, not the moving pointer.\n   - Positive control: seed81's published #1042 result is reproduced exactly from `certificates/checkpoints/frontier1042.json`.\n2. **Seed81's own entry point is stale on main.** `make frontier1042-invoice-audit-verify` fails with `selected certificate path moved`, because it requires the *selected* certificate to be #1042's. Suggested one-line repair: read the frozen checkpoint. Not applied here; #1654 notes the same pattern in another capsule audit.\n3. **#1094's invoice arithmetic is unchanged from #1042.** The receipts differ in exactly 14 fields: three provenance hashes in the invoice, plus the idle-remainder profile and three counters in the owner receipt.\n4. **The profile agrees across five artifacts:**\n   - the certificate;\n   - the archived owner receipt;\n   - the package's `PROFILE.json`;\n   - the package's `data/PLAN.json`;\n   - `INDEPENDENT1094`'s owner-audited profile.\n5. **Binding gap, demonstrated with a well-formed mutant certificate.** The mutant takes `complex_lower + 1e-24`, the next grid point, and recomputes the bootstrap, all 47 outer slacks and both complex moment records with seed81's formulas. \u03ba is unchanged.\n\n| Layer | Mutant |\n|---|---|\n| Invoice/outer arithmetic (endpoint as data) | accepted |\n| `verify_selected_result.check` with `certificate_sha256` re-pinned | accepted (a \u03ba edit is still rejected) |\n| `scripts/verify_frontier1094.py` | no reference to the #1094 certificate, the selected record or `certificate_sha256` |\n| Candidate stage `complex-t16-rare-pattern-exchanges/verify.py` | binds only status, \u03ba and the replay's profile (to `PROFILE.json`); never names `complex_lower`, `bootstrap`, `outer`, `moments` |\n| Exact moment (`selected-suppliers-de-diagnostic` enclosure) | **rejected**: residual lower bound 1.62\u00b710\u207b\u00b2\u2074 > 0 (certified endpoint: upper bound \u22121.30\u00b710\u207b\u00b2\u2074) |\n\nSo the record's hash pin says which bytes are selected, and the cold replay says which \u03ba is reproduced. Nothing on `make frontier1094-verify` says those bytes are the replay's output.\n\n**This is not a defect in the current certificate.** The archived replay output `candidate/strict/ASSEMBLY.json` and the published `RESULT.json` `assembly_sha256` both equal the certificate (`1122cb3a\u2026`).\n\n### Proposed handoff (not applied: selected reproduce script, maintainer decision)\n```python\nrequire(sha(work/'candidate/strict/ASSEMBLY.json') ==\n        read(ROOT/'certificates/selected-result.json')['certificate_sha256'],\n        'Replay output is the selected certificate')\n```\nAlternatively, use a parsed-JSON comparison such as #474's `check_selected_replay.py` helper. The package shows the requirement holds on the published replay output and rejects the mutant.\n\nStatically, `verify_frontier1042/942/890/799.py` also contain no reference to their certificates. They were not audited further.\n\n### Not checked\n- **Cold replay:** no fresh cold `make frontier1094-verify` was run, with or without the line; it needs the long #1042 baseline.\n- **Inherited obligations:** semantic receipt content (words, owners, hosting) is taken as data, and the native, all-size, precision, analytic and H1\u2013H5 obligations are inherited unchanged.\n- **Environment:** run on Windows with CPython 3.14. The registered 3.12 replay was not run locally; `--check-only` and the research tests pass.\n\n### Credit and related work\n- **#474** (artuskg, open) first identified this class of gap for the historical gen4 record. No priority is claimed for the pattern.\n- **#1277** (merged) covers this replay's ancestry binding; **#1654** (open) is its tooling-family overlap receipt. Neither adds a certificate comparison.\n- **Reused unchanged:** Wronskode (seed81 recheck) and Navinor (DE moment enclosure).\n- **Selected scripts and composition:** Douglas Colkitt.\n- **Construction:** Rohan Arun (#1094), with Jeremy Kothe's k8/T16 construction and the credited supplier lineage.\n\nSubstantial AI assistance: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5), one donated session, no subagents, no independent human review. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
